A conversion whose target is a pointer type. The target *Dst must be
parenthesized as (*Dst)(x): written bare, *Dst(x) parses as a dereference
*(Dst(x)), a conversion of the source to the value type Dst, then a deref,
which does not type-check. A named pointer type P (= *Dst) is the convertible
source, so whatever produces a P satisfies a *Dst demand through the conversion.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type Dst struct{ x int }

type P *Dst

//plumb:build
var _ *Dst = (P)(nil)

//plumb:build
func Use(d *Dst) int { return d.x }
